<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sainte-Marie-aux-Mines</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sainte-Marie-aux-Mines is a town in a valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haut-rhin">Haut-Rhin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In the sixteenth century its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines were among the richest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and the valley was divided between the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> and the lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lordship-of-rappoltstein">Ribeaupierre</a>. The town later became a centre of textile manufacture and is known for its international mineral fair.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sainte-marie-aux-mines.jpg" alt="Sainte-Marie-aux-Mines" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Chenal · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sainte_Marie-aux-Mines_016.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
